{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Goblin Salvage Project: the map marks each objective and the tracker follows it",
  "contract": [
    "Requires CoA.SendDisplayPatches=1 (the default).",
    "The questline 176000-176014 is new, so the client has no QuestSuperTrack row and the server had no quest_poi row for it: the world map and the tracker showed nothing. rev_20261023_51 adds both.",
    "A real client asks CMSG_QUEST_POI_QUERY (483) for the quests in its log and reads SMSG_QUEST_POI_QUERY_RESPONSE (484): quest count, quest id, POI count, then per POI its id, objective index, map, area, floor, priority, flags, point count and integer points, in quest_poi id order. For 176001 One Goblin's Junk it must hold the turn-in pin on Fizzlebolt Gearwhistle, then the item areas.",
    "The 3.3.5a client draws the selected quest's areas in WorldMapBlobFrame:DrawQuestBlob (0x58ED80), which copies each POI's points plus three closing entries into a 15-entry stack buffer: a POI may hold at most 12 points. Blizzard's quest_poi_points never exceed 12; a 14-point Field Testing area overwrote the frame's own pointer and crashed the client when the map opened.",
    "The login patch stream sends coa_client_quest_super_track rows as SMSG_PATCH_QUEST_SUPER_TRACK (1727) and coa_client_super_track rows as SMSG_PATCH_SUPER_TRACK (1726). Row 33401 (176001) must point objective 0-2 at the gearbox, Shredder and canister nodes and its completion at node 20900 on Fizzlebolt's spawn; the Horde row 33414 (176014) completes at the client's own Baron Revilgaz node 131, which stays unpatched.",
    "These are data assertions on the bytes the server sends; the harness cannot see how the client draws the map areas or the diamond."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 60000,
